  "local_policies": [
    "Kaahrj retains each original actual Battlecry enemy minion selection on its own native Deathrattle attachment. Original source/target allocations, residence, Battlecry id/role/window and frozen printed intrinsic base copy stay typed. Repeated original Battlecries append separate selections, each later actual Deathrattle emits all saved copies through ordinary attributed summons/quantity/capacity. Original later buffs/transform/death do not change accepted base material. The delayed printed recipe uses the existing remembered_copy/base path; every actual attributed summon must match a real executed native selected-copy Deathrattle, its original immutable subject material and current Deathrattle recipient. Immediate board_copy capture-window checks remain unchanged.",
    "Najak records original selected enemy residence and previous controller before ordinary capture/control publication. Original native Deathrattle returns the same still-present physical minion to that captured controller, independent of source later controller or owner; later same-id reentry cannot borrow the old link. Current face/control changes within original board residence do not rewrite the subject. Full-board control/departure follows ordinary writer; selection memory is not an invented success receipt. Returning an original dormant resident with space and an active resident to a full board uses the same shared existing return writer as removed control layers: the former transfers, the latter is destroyed. Dormant plus full destination remains an explicit original unsupported death-policy error with atomic rollback, recorded for later CN boundary work.",
    "Typed selected native memory adds one empty-default tuple; every original memory profile, clone/inheritance/silence/bounce/restore path remains under existing lifecycle and validation. Original active Battlecry or Deathrattle proof binds new work; unknown/future/foreign allocations or mixed payload roles reject, not silent white bodies.",
    "Celestia listens to original completed non-countered opponent minion play, resolves its original entry residence, and uses current live physical copy transformation. Departed/dormant/doomed original entry is skipped rather than borrowing a new same-id body or guessing its last local material; exact edge behavior remains local pending CN.",
    "Nameless One captures its original chosen minion, becomes a current4/4 copy through ordinary transform, then captured silence applies to that original target. Recipient old reference reset does not redirect silence; target leaving/reentering between notifications makes old silence stale. No new copy/lifecycle executor.",
    "Plaguemaw uses actual frozen friendly death keywords, including granted Taunt, and ordinary base resurrection with finite pre-entry removal of local Taunt. Printed body/intrinsic composition/Jade/permanent recipe and normal quantity/placement/capacity/reborn remain shared. No original local buffs or retained native selection memory are copied into a fresh body. External continuous auras still follow existing aura refresh policies."
  ],
  "unsupported_or_unconfirmed": [
    "complete past732 source binding",
    "exact CN copy/selected-memory/linked control and pre-entry Taunt aura windows",
    "formal current pool version and CN legality",
    "version/hotfix alignment"
  ]
}
